WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:05.260
I am sick and tired of these efforts to privatize
a precious thing we need, public education.

00:00:05.260 --> 00:00:09.370
I know we're not supposed to be saying hate,
our teachers taught us not to,

00:00:09.370 --> 00:00:12.120
I hate the privatizers, I want to stop them.

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:15.190
Speaking recently before the country's largest
union

00:00:15.190 --> 00:00:20.520
New York City Mayor Bill de Blasio came out
against the very concept of charter schools.

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:27.660
Too many Republicans but also too many Democrats
have been cozy with the charter schools

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:29.740
let's be blunt about it.

00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:34.420
De Blasio's opinion as a fourth tier Democratic
presidential candidate doesn't matter much

00:00:34.420 --> 00:00:38.039
but what's disturbing is the extent to which
his anti-charter animus

00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:40.900
is rapidly becoming a core value in the Democratic
party.

00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:43.400
As the head of the nation's largest school
system,

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:47.840
de Blasio's prejudices are also having a direct
impact on individual lives.

00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:54.299
In New York City 123 thousand students out
of a public school system of 1.1 million

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:56.020
attend charter schools.

00:00:56.020 --> 00:01:00.520
Unsurprisingly the mayor's remarks drew hot
fire from the hometown tabloids.

00:01:11.580 --> 00:01:14.200
-snarled the New York Daily News, and-

00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:30.260
the hostility that New York progressives,

00:01:30.260 --> 00:01:33.930
especially white New York progressives,
have toward charters

00:01:33.930 --> 00:01:38.880
is already taking its toll on poor minority
kids stuck in failing districts.

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:40.600
The state legislature last month

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:44.400
elected not to lift the cap on the number
of charters allowed in New York City

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:46.780
despite overwhelming demand from parents.

00:01:46.780 --> 00:01:50.280
As local political personality and columnist
Errol Louis noted

00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:52.820
in the 2017-18 school year,

00:01:52.820 --> 00:01:57.110
about 59% of black students attending charters
passed the state math test

00:01:57.110 --> 00:02:00.760
compared with only 25% in regular district
schools.

00:02:00.760 --> 00:02:04.880
One charter school in the Bronx recently saw
every single one of its eighth graders

00:02:04.890 --> 00:02:07.370
earn a perfect score on the state algebra
exam

00:02:07.370 --> 00:02:10.780
despite being situated in the nations' poorest
congressional district.

00:02:10.780 --> 00:02:14.980
Half of kids attending traditional public
schools in the same district failed the test.

00:02:14.980 --> 00:02:19.020
53% of the charters' kids are African American,
38% are Latino,

00:02:19.020 --> 00:02:21.960
81% are low income, free and reduced lunch,

00:02:21.960 --> 00:02:29.320
and they're outscoring the traditional public
schools in every measurable dimension,

00:02:29.320 --> 00:02:33.000
I understand where there are problems like,
you know,

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:36.200
there are 53 thousand people on this waiting
list and so forth

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:39.240
but there's nothing you can learn from them?

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:43.260
We again I say we partner with the ones that
share those values of inclusion

00:02:43.269 --> 00:02:45.980
we work with them, best practices are shared
both ways.

00:02:45.980 --> 00:02:47.700
I think there are some charter schools that
do the work,

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:50.480
I think there are some charter schools that
are test prep factories,

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:52.599
I think there are some charter schools that
are exclusionary

00:02:52.599 --> 00:02:54.609
and that goes against everything I believe
in.

00:02:54.609 --> 00:02:56.400
Former Congressman Beto O'Rourke,

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:59.019
who used to be a full-throated supporter of
charters,

00:02:59.019 --> 00:03:02.319
was the only one of the ten candidates at
the same teachers union conference

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:06.620
brave enough to suggest even that there is
a place for public nonprofit charter schools.

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:08.880
But Beto quickly got to the but.

00:03:08.880 --> 00:03:11.940
But private charter schools and voucher programs,

00:03:11.940 --> 00:03:14.940
not a single dime of my administration will
go to them.

00:03:14.940 --> 00:03:17.820
What used to be a fairly mainstream democratic
idea,

00:03:17.829 --> 00:03:20.919
championed by the likes of Barack Obama, Joe
Biden

00:03:20.919 --> 00:03:23.900
and pre-presidential campaign Senator Corey
Booker

00:03:23.900 --> 00:03:28.529
has now become something candidates feel like
they need to furiously backpedal from

00:03:28.529 --> 00:03:30.189
and according to one recent survey,

00:03:30.189 --> 00:03:35.230
those reformist tendencies are not likely
to be seen again from a democrat anytime soon.

00:03:35.230 --> 00:03:36.659
Bill de Blasio's career

00:03:36.659 --> 00:03:40.989
has been marked by the extent to which he's
willing to sell out his constituents,

00:03:40.989 --> 00:03:43.739
in this case poor kids in failing schools,

00:03:43.739 --> 00:03:46.579
in order to advance his own political career.

00:03:46.580 --> 00:03:49.780
Sadly that puts him in the mainstream of the
modern democratic party.

